TUDOR TIMES WEEKLY =E2=80=94 week of 18 September 1525
Your trusted source for crown, court and countryside.

THIS WEEK IN HISTORY:
  * Henry's children Mary I, Elizabeth I and Edward VI each took the throne i=
n turn.
  * England's currency in this period reckoned in pounds, marks, shillings an=
d pence.
  * A royal progress could move the entire court between palaces for months a=
t a time.

COURT WHISPERS: New French fashions arrive at Greenwich =E2=80=94 ruffs are s=
aid to be growing.

WEATHER: Grey, with a chance of beheadings. (Editorial humour; no offence int=
ended.)

